.. par:parameter:: Monitor:level

   :Summary: :s:`Level of information written to stdout`
   :Type:    :par:typefmt:`string`
   :Default: :d:`"medium"`
   :Scope:     :c:`Cello`

   :e:`This parameter controls the verbosity of output during a running simulation. Possible values are "high", "medium", "low", and "none".`

----

.. par:parameter:: Monitor:mute_list

   :Summary: :s:`Which monitor output components to mute`
   :Type:    :par:typefmt:`list ( string )`
   :Default: :d:`[]`
   :Scope:     :c:`Cello`

   :e:`List of monitor output components, such as "Performance", "Solver", "Simulation", to mute. Default is the empty list with no components muted.`

----

.. par:parameter:: Monitor:only_list

   :Summary: :s:`Which monitor output components to write, muting others`
   :Type:    :par:typefmt:`list ( string )`
   :Default: :d:`[]`
   :Scope:     :c:`Cello`

   :e:`List of monitor output components, such as "Performance", "Solver", "Simulation", to include in monitoring output. Analogous to "solo" in audio mixing, it effectively mutes all components not listed. Default is the empty list, for which all components are active except those in the mute_list.)`
